  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe dry weather to start the weekend will continue into Sunday \nmorning for most areas. This will occur as high pressure tracking \nacross the area will slowly track off the coast through tonight. As \nthe sfc high pushes east of the area, temperatures and humidity will \nincrease some from previous days. A shortwave trough approaching \nfrom the northwest will start to increase the potential for showers \nwith a few thunderstorms starting later Sunday morning. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nShowers with some thunderstorms will increase in coverage for Sunday \nafternoon and evening as a weak shortwave trough crosses the region \nduring the peak heating of the day. Another batch of more organized \nshowers will track across the area as another shortwave tracks \nsoutheast along a stalled frontal boundary across the region. This \nwill become the theme for the coming work week as a ridge develops \nover the Lower Mississippi Valley to the SE CONUS. Northwest flow \nevents over the region will continue along the northeastern \nperiphery of the ridge through the week. This will result in several \nrounds of showers and thunderstorms through the week at different \ntimes. The greatest potential for severe weather is expected for \nWednesday when a potent shortwave trough will dive southeast across \nthe region. This is still in day 5, so a lot can change and any \nchanges in the track of the trough are certainly possible, resulting \nin storms further south or north of current forecast.",
